<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- The miwb motion-brief Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs; docs/EVAL-LOOP.md,
     "Cross-engine gate") in the face of the typst template ({font}) at 12 pt (size 24 half points; MIWB-FORM-001, LBR
     9004(f), at least 12-point type); Body Text in exact 27.6 pt line boxes (552 twips, typst pitch-body; LBR 9004(f),
     double-spaced, the exemplars' 27.6 pt pitch) with a half-inch first-line indent (typst para-indent); single lines
     in 13.8 pt boxes (276 twips, typst pitch-single); footnotes at 12 pt in single lines, 4 pt apart (typst note-gap);
     letter page (MIWB-FORM-011), 1 in margins. Added or replaced here, as the typst template sets them: "Body Text
     Note" (no widow control, for a paragraph that anchors a footnote), "List Letter" (the letter hanging in a half-inch
     box half an inch in), Block Text (half an inch in, on the body pitch, no space of its own), the three heading
     levels on the body pitch with no space of their own (printed as the filter writes them, no style capitals; h1
     centred bold, h2 bold, h3 bold italic), Footnote Text (the recipe's, without keepLines: typst splits a long note
     across pages), and the footer: the page number at 11 pt in a single line (a PAGE field), 731 twips above the page
     foot so its baseline stands where typst sets it (footer-descent 30 %). The last section (the brief in support)
     restarts its page numbers at 1; the motion's section ends where the filter writes it
     (docx/miwb-motion-brief.lua). Caption, title and signature carry their own spacing. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
